"P900659154" "The Book of Old"
// DetailString :
"P1760335424" "This book seems to be ancient. The text is unreadable, in a language that {HeroName} couldn't understand. The cover was held on by the barest of threads. Either it was well read of the robots were not very careful in extracting it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1883448076" "(The third book of Trilogy opens to a random page) {HeroName} was beginning to miss Mercenary's company, even as gruff as he was. {Hero.Gender=male He|She} missed the jokes, the constant movie references, but {Hero.Gender=male he|she} knew that Mercenary had some things to deal with that were best dealt with on his own. Mercenary promised to be back and soon, but that didn't make the separation any easier. {HeroName}'s thoughts turned to Epoch as {Hero.Gender=male he|she} ventured on the road back to the valley. Epoch had taught him many things, but dealing with loss would be the final lesson he would teach."
// AcceptString :
"P1357556066" "Turn the page of chapter 7 in the final book."
// SendOffString :
"P1712413809" "{HeroName}'s eyes never looked up from the road {hero.gender=male he|she} tread upon back to the valley. {hero.gender=male His|Her} first indication of any trouble was the scent of burning wood. {hero.gender=male He|She} lifted {hero.gender=male his|her} eyes to see columns of smoke rising up from {hero.gender=male his|her} childhood home. {hero.gender=male His|Her} first thought was not {hero.gender=male his|her} own homestead, but Epoch's home on the hill. {hero.gender=male He|She} noted it was fully engulfed in flames. Whatever secrets it held were being lost to the fire. {hero.gender=male He|She} saw some robots located just outside the house. If Infinity was after anything of value, these robots would likely still be carrying it."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P68510524" "Defeat the robots to recover whatever they found"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3897550424" "{HeroName}'s eyes never looked up from the road {hero.gender=male he|she} tread upon back to the valley. {hero.gender=male His|Her} first indication of any trouble was the scent of burning wood. {hero.gender=male He|She} lifted {hero.gender=male his|her} eyes to see columns of smoke rising up from his childhood home. {hero.gender=male His|Her} first thought was not his own homestead, but Epoch's home on the hill. {hero.gender=male He|She} noted it was fully engulfed in flames. Whatever secrets it held were being lost to the fire. {hero.gender=male He|She} saw some robots located just outside the house. If Infinity was after anything of value, these robots would likely still be carrying it."
